{
 "schema": 1,
 "name": "Casting Desecrate always triggers Shadowstorm, even when the cone misses everything (#9492)",
 "contract": "Shadowstorm 520277's Description reads 'Casting Desecrate always triggers Shadowstorm', an unconditional cast-gated clause contrasted against the damage-chance-gated Pommel Smash clause in the same tooltip. Before the fix, the trigger ran through the native spell_proc dispatcher (HitMask 9283: normal/crit/block/absorb/full-block only, excluding miss/dodge/parry) and a C++ Direct(event) check requiring nonzero damage, so a Desecrate cone that connected with nothing never produced a Shadowstorm. Desecrate (680518) is SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_MELEE, so its hit roll resolves through Unit::MeleeSpellHitResult (dodge/parry/miss tables), not the magic hit-chance path; forcing a deterministic dodge needs QA Test 100% Dodge 10020 (SPELL_AURA_MOD_DODGE_PERCENT) on the victim, and set_aura only resolves a player actor, so the target is a second PvP-flagged, opposing-faction player ('defender', an Undead, so a same-faction 'target_friendly' Human pair does not need a duel) rather than a fixture creature. The trigger is gated on the Shadowstorm talent/passive 520277 itself: a Witch Hunter who never learned it must cast Desecrate without ever producing a Shadowstorm. The Witch Hunter fixture omits expertise_rating: expertise directly reduces the victim's dodge/parry chance, and a large expertise rating would cancel out the forced QA Test 100% Dodge aura just as reliably as it would a real one, so only melee/spell hit rating (which guards against a plain miss, not dodge) are kept.",
 "timeout_ms": 90000,
